.\" jarvisagent(1) — JarvisAgent user manual
.\" Generated for JarvisAgent 0.9
.TH JARVISAGENT 1 "April 2026" "JarvisAgent 0.9" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
jarvisAgent \- parallel AI\-driven automation engine with visual workflow editor
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jarvisagent.sh
.RB [ \-\-studio " | " \-\-engine ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.br
.B jarvisAgent\-studio
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.br
.B jarvisAgent\-engine
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
JarvisAgent is a C++ backend / React frontend application for parallel
AI\-driven automation.
Its engine core dispatches many concurrent AI requests in parallel \(em think
requirements analysis across hundreds of items, stock\-portfolio deep\-research
across every position, or chapter\-by\-chapter processing of entire PDF books.
.PP
Office documents (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, PDF) are automatically converted to
Markdown via Microsoft MarkItDown \(em and chunked when too large \(em before
being sent to the AI.
JarvisAgent is file\-oriented by design: all inputs, outputs, and intermediate
results live on disk, making it a natural fit for engineering environments with
large file landscapes.
.PP
Workflows let you chain serial and parallel tasks \(em AI calls, Python scripts,
shell commands, or native C++ \(em in a visual graph editor with various trigger
types (manual, cron, file_watch).
.PP
The application ships in two editions \(em \fBStudio\fR (full developer IDE)
and \fBEngine\fR (lean production server) \(em each with its own binary and
security profile.
See
.B EDITIONS
below.
.PP
The application ships with an ncurses terminal UI for local or SSH sessions,
a browser\-based React dashboard for remote monitoring, and a visual workflow
editor.
It compiles and runs on Linux, macOS, and Windows.
.
.SH EDITIONS
JarvisAgent builds as two distinct binaries selected at build time:
.PP
.TS
l l l
l l l.
	\fBj9t Studio (default)\fR	\fBj9t Engine\fR
Binary	jarvisAgent\-studio	jarvisAgent\-engine
Purpose	Developer workstation	Production server
Network	Localhost only	LAN / internet
Browser UI auth	None (localhost)	Session cookie (after MCP key login)
MCP / API auth	MCP API key	MCP API key
Webhook auth	HMAC\-SHA256 (optional)	HMAC\-SHA256 (mandatory)
RBAC	3 roles on MCP keys	3 roles on MCP keys / sessions / gateway
Rate limit	None	100 req/min per IP, burst 20
Audit log	None	log/security.txt (10 MB x 5)
Body limit	None	Configurable (default 10 MB)
Workflow CRUD	Full	Not available (compile\-time removed)
AI assistant	Full	Not available (compile\-time removed)
AI JCWF gen	Full	Not available (compile\-time removed)
Attack surface	Full feature set	Minimal \(em runtime + monitoring
.TE
.PP
Studio is designed for single\-developer use on a local machine.
Engine is designed for production deployments behind an API gateway.
See
.B SECURITY
for details.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Installed launcher (the jarvisagent command, and the AppImage / Flatpak / macOS .app / Windows jarvisagent.bat equivalents)
.TP
.BI \-\-home " DIR"
Working directory to create and run in (default ~/JarvisAgent).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-browser
Do not open the dashboard in a browser (a no-op where the launcher opens none, e.g. AppImage/Flatpak).
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-\-version
Forwarded to the binary, which prints and exits before any first-run setup (no working directory or Python venv is created).
.SS Source-tree launcher (jarvisagent.sh, for running from a build tree)
.TP
.BR \-\-studio ", " \-\-engine
Select the edition (default Studio).
.TP
.BR \-\-debug ", " \-\-release
Select the build configuration (default Release).
.SS Binary flags (jarvisAgent\-studio / jarvisAgent\-engine)
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print the version number and exit.
.PP
Unknown options cause an error message and a non\-zero exit code, in both the launchers and the binary.
.
